            <ArticleTitle>Pursuit of Noncovalent Interactions for Strategic Site-Selective Catalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>609-615</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.accounts.6b00613</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Selective reactions on structures of high complexity can move beyond the mind's eye and proof-of-principle. Enhanced understanding of noncovalent interactions and their interdependence, revealed through analysis of multiple parameters, should accelerate the discovery of efficient reactions in highly complex molecular environments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
